  <p>AI models are changing fast.</p>
  <p>ChatGPT. Claude. Gemini. Llama. Mistral. Local models. Future agents we haven't even seen yet.</p>
  <p>But there's one problem:</p>

  <div style="background:var(--panel);border-left:4px solid var(--accent-bar);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:18px 20px;margin:24px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--fg);">Your context does not travel with you.</p>
  </div>

  <p>Your memory, rules, project knowledge, workflows, preferences, and operating style get trapped inside each platform.</p>
  <p>That is the problem CAS is designed to solve.</p>

  <h2 style="color:var(--accent);border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline);padding-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;margin-top:36px;">CAS — Context Architecture System</h2>
  <p>An open standard for portable, user-owned AI context.</p>

  <div style="background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--accent-bar);padding:24px 28px;border-radius:10px;margin:28px 0;text-align:center;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:0.06em;">The metaphor is simple:</p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:15px;color:var(--fg);">The model is the body. &nbsp; The context is the shell.</p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);">Like a hermit crab changing bodies while keeping its shell, CAS gives users a durable context structure that can move across models, agents, tools, and future AI systems.</p>
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:0.04em;">One Shell. Any Body. Forever.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 style="color:var(--accent);border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline);padding-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;margin-top:36px;">What CAS is not</h2>

  <div style="background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--hairline);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:15px;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--fg);"><strong style="color:var(--link);">Not another chatbot.</strong></p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--fg);"><strong style="color:var(--link);">Not another agent.</strong></p>
    <p style="margin:0;color:var(--fg);"><strong style="color:var(--link);">Not a wrapper around one model.</strong></p>
  </div>

  <p>It is a context architecture: a structured way to preserve identity, projects, knowledge, rules, workflows, memory, and reusable instructions <em>outside</em> any single AI vendor.</p>

  <h2 style="color:var(--accent);border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline);padding-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;margin-top:36px;">The goal</h2>
  <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:2.2;">
    <li><strong>User-owned context.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Model freedom.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Portable intelligence.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>No vendor lock-in.</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <p>I believe the next major layer of AI infrastructure will not just be better models.</p>

  <div style="background:var(--panel);border-left:4px solid var(--accent-bar);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:18px 20px;margin:24px 0;">
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:var(--fg);">It will be better context.</p>
  </div>

